Answer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2024-jun-q1a","p":5,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(a)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":null,"marks":4,"questionText":"The table below shows price elasticity of demand for bus tickets in London 2021 Explain one likely reason for the difference in the price elasticity of demand for the 18+ student bus ticket and the adult bus ticket.","topics":["1-2-3-price-income-cross-elasticities-of-demand"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["price elasticity of demand","determinants of PED","bus tickets"],"qpPage":2,"msPage":4,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2024-jun-q5a","p":33,"section":"A","questionNumber":"5(a)","parentQuestion":"5","choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"Chief Executive Elon Musk said “affordability” was the biggest barrier to Tesla reaching a far larger market. Before recent price cuts for its electric vehicles, he said, “We weren’t sure about what the price elasticity of demand was for Tesla. We found that even small changes in price have a big impact on demand.” In June 2023, Tesla further reduced the price of its Model 3 vehicle by £4 200 from £42 990. It has been forecast that the price cut will lead to a 15% increase in demand. Ceteris paribus, calculate the price elasticity of demand for the Model 3. You are advised to show your working.","topics":["1-2-3-price-income-cross-elasticities-of-demand"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["price elasticity of demand","calculation","Tesla"],"qpPage":10,"msPage":9,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2024-jun-q6c","p":33,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(c)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":4,"questionText":"With reference to Extract A, explain the likely numerical value for the income elasticity of demand for reusable cleaning products.","topics":["1-2-3-price-income-cross-elasticities-of-demand"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["income elasticity of demand","YED","normal good","calculation"],"qpPage":14,"msPage":14,"ctxPage":12,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2024-jun-q1a","p":23,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(a)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":null,"marks":5,"questionText":"With reference to Figure 1 and Extract A, explain what is meant by ‘price inelastic demand’ (line 8).","topics":["1-2-3-price-income-cross-elasticities-of-demand"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["price inelastic demand","PED","energy"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":4,"ctxPage":3,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2023-jun-q6a","p":32,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(a)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":5,"questionText":"With reference to Figure 1 and Extract A, explain the relationship between price elasticity of demand and total revenue.","topics":["1-2-3-price-income-cross-elasticities-of-demand"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["price elasticity of demand","total revenue","PED"],"qpPage":13,"msPage":12,"ctxPage":11,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2023-jun-q6c","p":4,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(c)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":8,"questionText":"With reference to the information provided, examine the likely numerical value of the cross elasticity of demand between UK online streaming services.","topics":["1-2-3-price-income-cross-elasticities-of-demand"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["cross elasticity of demand","XED","substitutes","streaming"],"qpPage":15,"msPage":13,"ctxPage":13,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2023-jun-q6d","p":32,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(d)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":4,"questionText":"Using examples from the information provided, explain what is meant by both ‘substitutes’ and ‘complementary goods’.","topics":["1-2-3-price-income-cross-elasticities-of-demand","1-2-2-demand"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["substitutes","complementary goods","cross e